questions.question_text:
The area of this circle is $85$ cm$^{2}$.
What is the radius, correct to $1$ decimal place?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=1]
\draw[thick] (0,0) circle (1.6);
\fill (0,0) circle (1.5pt);
\draw[dashed] (0,0) -- (40:1.6) node[midway,above left] {$r$};
\node[below] at (0,-1.85) {$A = 85\text{ cm}^{2}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The area of this circle is $45$ mm$^{2}$.
What is the diameter, correct to $1$ decimal place?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=1]
\draw[thick] (0,0) circle (1.6);
\fill (0,0) circle (1.5pt);
\draw[dashed] (-1.6,0) -- (1.6,0) node[midway,below] {$d$};
\node[below] at (0,-1.95) {$A = 45\text{ mm}^{2}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The area of this semicircle is $40$ m$^{2}$.
What is the radius, correct to $2$ decimal places?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=1]
\draw[thick] (-1.9,0) -- (1.9,0);
\draw[thick] (1.9,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=180,radius=1.9];
\fill (0,0) circle (1.5pt);
\draw[dashed] (0,0) -- (55:1.9) node[midway,above left] {$r$};
\node[below] at (0,-0.15) {$A = 40\text{ m}^{2}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The area of this quadrant is $9$ cm$^{2}$.
What is the radius, correct to $2$ decimal places?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=1]
\draw[thick] (0,0) -- (2.2,0);
\draw[thick] (0,0) -- (0,2.2);
\draw[thick] (2.2,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=90,radius=2.2];
\draw (0.28,0) -- (0.28,0.28) -- (0,0.28);
\fill (0,0) circle (1.5pt);
\node[left] at (0,1.1) {$r$};
\node[below] at (1.1,-0.35) {$A = 9\text{ cm}^{2}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The area of this sector is $24$ m$^{2}$.
What is the radius, correct to $2$ decimal places?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=1]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (P) at (0:2.4);
\coordinate (Q) at (40:2.4);
\draw[thick] (O) -- (P) node[midway,below] {$r$};
\draw[thick] (O) -- (Q);
\draw[thick] (P) arc[start angle=0,end angle=40,radius=2.4];
\pic[draw,"$40^{\circ}$",angle radius=0.55cm,angle eccentricity=2.2] {angle=P--O--Q};
\node at (1.2,-1.0) {$A = 24\text{ m}^{2}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The area of this sector is $96$ cm$^{2}$.
What is the angle $\theta$ at the centre, correct to the nearest degree?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=1]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (P) at (0:2.4);
\coordinate (Q) at (172:2.4);
\draw[thick] (O) -- (P) node[midway,below] {$8\text{ cm}$};
\draw[thick] (O) -- (Q);
\draw[thick] (P) arc[start angle=0,end angle=172,radius=2.4];
\pic[draw,"$\theta$",angle radius=0.62cm,angle eccentricity=1.9] {angle=P--O--Q};
\node at (1.2,-1.0) {$A = 96\text{ cm}^{2}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The area of this circle is $121\pi$ m$^{2}$.
What is the exact radius?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=1]
\draw[thick] (0,0) circle (1.6);
\fill (0,0) circle (1.5pt);
\draw[dashed] (0,0) -- (40:1.6) node[midway,above left] {$r$};
\node[below] at (0,-1.85) {$A = 121\pi\text{ m}^{2}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A circular pond of area $20$ m$^{2}$ sits at the centre of a circular lawn, and together they cover $80$ m$^{2}$.
What is the width $w$ of the ring of lawn, correct to $2$ decimal places?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=1]
\draw[thick] (0,0) circle (2.4);
\draw[thick] (0,0) circle (1.2);
\fill (0,0) circle (1.5pt);
\node at (0,-0.6) {$20\text{ m}^{2}$};
\draw[<->] (0,1.2) -- (0,2.4);
\node[right] at (0.08,1.8) {$w$};
\node[below] at (0,-2.55) {total area $= 80\text{ m}^{2}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A circle has the same area as a square of side $15$ cm.
What is the radius of the circle, correct to $2$ decimal places?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=1]
\draw[thick] (0,0) rectangle (2.4,2.4);
\node[below] at (1.2,0) {$15\text{ cm}$};
\draw[thick] (5,1.2) circle (1.35);
\fill (5,1.2) circle (1.5pt);
\draw[dashed] (5,1.2) -- (6.034,2.068) node[midway,above left] {$r$};
\node[below] at (5,-0.15) {equal areas};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
